  25: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
  26:     """
  27:     Dock train sprites onto station groups by matching coupler count, then orient via divider-color markers.
  28: 
  29:     Input structure:
  30:     - bg; colored stripes (edge + internal) partition grid into rectangular regions.
  31:     - Color 8 forms train bodies; color 9 marks both isolated stations and train-attached couplers.
  32:     - Stripe-colored pixels on trains are orientation markers.
  33: 
  34:     Rule:
  35:     - Stations = 8-connected 9-clusters not adjacent to any 8. Trains = components containing 8.
  36:     - Match train to station group where |couplers| == |station size|.
  37:     - Rotate/flip train so marker pixels face the same-color boundary stripe of the target region.
  38:     - Translate so couplers align exactly onto station cells; erase original position.
  39: 
  40:     Key insight: Coupler count selects the docking target; marker color encodes which boundary stripe to face, fixing the unique orientation.
